  "engagement_proof": {
    "bit_compare_vs_production_kernel": "f16 outputs of split+reduce vs the production single-pass kernel: qkv/o/gate_up bit-identical at every S; down differs on exactly 1 of 896 outputs, max 1 f16 ulp, identical at S=2/4/8 (the reorder is absorbed by the f16 rounding on three shapes and flips one output on K=4864)",
    "timing_scaling": "split kernel wall scales with S (gate_up 2.15-2.47x at S=8); a non-engaged variant would time and compare identical to base",
    "spirv_gate": "all 24 default qmm_vec variants compile to byte-identical SPIR-V from the variant source (glslc -O --target-env=vulkan1.3, old vs new sha256-compared); the split and reduce variants compile new code paths only under -DQMM_VEC_Q4_SPLITK",
    "why_bit_identity_here_is_not_a_contradiction": "split-K changes the accumulation ORDER by design; on these shapes the reordered f32 sums round to the same f16 bits almost everywhere, which is why the accuracy impact is measured at <=1 ulp instead of assumed"
  },
  "accuracy_statement": "Measured precision change vs the current production kernel: max 1 f16 ulp on 1 of 12672 layer-chain outputs (down), 0 elsewhere, at every split count. The f64-RNE model-level reference comparison from the original assignment was NOT run (needs the wheel; cut with the model-level legs by the receipt-only redirect). The isolated bit/ulp compare against the current kernel is the measured precision evidence; the current kernel's own distance to the f64 reference is documented in receipts/2026-09-11-q4-decode-pair-map.",
  "model_level_not_run": {
    "what": "no wheel build, no bench_decode legs, no generated-id digests at the 30/262/1053 legs",
    "why": "parent redirect on the isolated result: +52.9% chain time at the BEST split count already fails the >=3% gain bar by orders of magnitude, and any split count moves the pinned digests by construction (order change), so the digest outcome could not compensate",
    "harness_ready": "run_splitk_legs.py / run_accuracy_arm.py / compare_accuracy.py / window_legs.sh are committed on this branch for a future run if the isolated picture ever changes"
  },
